<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Rukh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1409">1409</a>–<a href="/years/1447">1447</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Rukh was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a> from 1409 to 1447, governing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>. His reign brought relative stability and a flourishing of Persian art and literature. Accounts of the Timurid Empire treat his long rule as a period of consolidation before the empire's fragmentation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shah-rukh.jpg" alt="Shah Rukh" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1435-1436 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Contemporary_portrait_of_Shah_Rukh,_painted_in_his_lifetime_in_1435-36,_by_commission_of_his_son_Ibrahim_Sultan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Qara Yusuf's death in 1420 <b>Shah Rukh</b> beat Qara Iskander in 1420–21 and briefly occupied Tabriz, beat him again in 1429, and in a third expedition of 1434–35 installed Iskander's brother Jahan Shah as vassal.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-qoyunlu">Qara Qoyunlu · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Yet his successors, above all <b>Shah Rukh</b> (r. 1405–1447, sole ruler from 1409) and his son Ulugh Beg (governor of Samarkand from 1409 and briefly ruler, 1447–1449), invested heavily in rebuilding agriculture, irrigation, urban infrastructure and commerce in the Transoxianan and Khorasanian heartlands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Timur conquered Mazandaran in 1392 and deported the family, but <b>Shah Rukh</b> restored them.</blockquote><a href="/state/marashi-dynasty">Mar'ashi dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
